---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getProjectById } from '../../../data/projects';

const project = getProjectById('disaster-recovery');

if (!project) {
  throw new Error('Backup & Recovery project data could not be found.');
}
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Backup & Recovery Platform"
  description="An operational resilience platform providing automated backups, recovery assurance, monitoring and daily management reporting."
>
<section class="project-hero">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Infrastructure Resilience Case Study</p>
<h1>Backup & Recovery Platform</h1>
<p class="project-summary">
A production-style resilience capability combining automated backups,
recovery assurance, monitoring visibility and operational reporting.
The objective is not only protecting data, but proving recovery readiness.
</p>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<div class="container content-grid">
<div>
<p class="eyebrow">The Challenge</p>
<h2>Backups are only useful when recovery confidence is measurable.</h2>
</div>
<div class="prose">
<p>
A reliable infrastructure platform requires more than storing backup files.
It requires visibility, validation and repeatable operational processes.
</p>
<p>
This project creates an operational resilience capability across a
multi-host environment using automation, monitoring and evidence-based reporting.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section section-soft">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Operational Workflow</p>
<h2>From backup execution to management confidence.</h2>
<div class="architecture">
<div>Backup automation</div>
<div>Prometheus metrics</div>
<div>Grafana visibility</div>
<div>Daily management email</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Recovery Assurance</p>
<h2>Measuring resilience, not assuming it.</h2>
<div class="grid capability-grid">
<article class="card"><h3>Backup Operations</h3><p>Automated backups provide controlled recovery points across managed infrastructure.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Repository Integrity</h3><p>Integrity checks provide evidence that backup repositories remain healthy.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Replication Health</h3><p>Off-host replication improves resilience against local infrastructure failure.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Recovery Validation</h3><p>Recovery processes are monitored and validated to improve confidence.</p></article>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section section-soft">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Management Visibility</p>
<h2>Turning technical health into operational reporting.</h2>
<div class="prose">
<p>
The platform generates daily management reporting by combining backup health,
recovery information and operational status into a concise automated brief.
</p>
<p>
This provides visibility for decision making without requiring management to
review technical dashboards or individual systems.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Operational Maturity</p>
<h2>Building resilience through visibility, assurance and ownership.</h2>
<div class="prose">
<p><strong>Visibility:</strong> Recovery readiness is exposed through monitoring dashboards.</p>
<p><strong>Assurance:</strong> Backup health, integrity and replication are measured.</p>
<p><strong>Communication:</strong> Daily reporting connects engineering outcomes with operational decisions.</p>
<p><strong>Ownership:</strong> Automation reduces dependency on individual knowledge.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<p class="eyebrow">Engineering Outcome</p>
<h2>Turning backups into resilience.</h2>
<div class="prose">
<p>
This project demonstrates that reliable infrastructure is not defined by
whether backups exist. It is defined by whether recovery capability is
visible, measurable and repeatable.
</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

</BaseLayout>
